{:edb/db-before-t 2045 :edb/db-after-t 2046 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535358 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:44:26.227Z" 13194139535358 true] [17592186119845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345708 13194139535358 true] [17592186119845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345715 13194139535358 true] [17592186119846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345694 13194139535358 true] [17592186119846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345701 13194139535358 true] [17592186120073 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535358 true] [17592186120073 1100 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." 13194139535358 true] [17592186120073 1100 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $a_{1} - 2a_{2} = 0$.\n2. $x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} = 0$ only if $x_{1} = x_{2} = 0$.\n3. The set ${a_{1}, a_{2}}$ is linearly independent." 13194139535358 false] [17592186120073 1145 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345694 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345695 13194139535358 true] [17592186345694 1089 "q-105308" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345694 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535358 true] [17592186345694 1100 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." 13194139535358 true] [17592186345694 1113 #uuid "272ae49c-9056-5da6-9688-ea58ac11f9c1" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345694 1145 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-16{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true." 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345696 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345697 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345698 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345699 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345700 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1041 "selection" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345700 13194139535358 true] [17592186345695 1110 #uuid "02d6925b-83d0-5682-b2df-8f48730e6d89" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345696 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345696 1111 #uuid "4e06061b-ccdb-5199-bbf5-9e833ef7c247" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345697 1034 "I only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345697 1111 #uuid "11930f00-5e4d-5b5b-b21c-251f48cea6d7" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345698 1034 "III only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345698 1111 #uuid "93d6df55-03b0-513a-ad51-c02435df9eca" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345699 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345699 1111 #uuid "a6caa2b7-ff97-55b3-8903-58b464f3a03c" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345700 1034 "II only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345700 1111 #uuid "a3b19f5c-26c1-57ce-88f0-0946f12bbc8f" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345701 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345702 13194139535358 true] [17592186345701 1089 "q-105310" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345701 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535358 true] [17592186345701 1100 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." 13194139535358 true] [17592186345701 1113 #uuid "62abef76-8742-588b-baa5-5503f357b61a" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345701 1145 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 15 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true." 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345703 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345704 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345705 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345706 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345707 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1041 "selection" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345707 13194139535358 true] [17592186345702 1110 #uuid "0ac2ed5a-52d4-5966-b66d-bf746a1a0dfe" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345703 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345703 1111 #uuid "8d7e3bdc-56ae-540b-a563-de3215d488a6" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345704 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535358 true] [17592186345704 1111 #uuid "c9caf19d-a350-5b0d-9e8e-56839cea5796" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345705 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535358 true] [17592186345705 1103 #edb/ref 1759218